      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vernon_Township%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The township’s first Masonic Lodge, founded in 1820, was named Mount Vernon after Washington’s Virginia home.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vernon_Township%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Mountain Creek, once known as Great Gorge and Vernon Valley, opened in 1972 and remains a popular ski resort and water park.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vernon_Township%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Hidden Valley, New Jersey’s only downhill ski area, closed in 2013 and now operates as the National Winter Activity Center.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vernon_Township%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Vernon Township Historical Society, founded in 1970, preserves local heritage through sites like Black Creek Site and Switch Schoolhouse.",
